<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rudrasimha III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">4th–5th century CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rudrasimha III was the last ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-satraps">Western Satraps</a> of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, reigning in the late 4th and early 5th centuries CE. Around 395 to 415 he was defeated by the Gupta emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chandragupta-ii">Chandragupta II</a>, who annexed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malwa">Malwa</a>, ending three centuries of Saka rule in the region and giving the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gupta-empire">Guptas</a> access to the ports of the western coast.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rudrasimha-iii.jpg" alt="Rudrasimha III" width="320" height="155" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhadramukhas_ruler_Rudrasimha_III_Circa_385-415_CE.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
